\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Why the completeness is quoted in two strata. \emph  {(a)}\nobreakspace  {}The 21{} directly injected Class\nobreakspace  {}A windows, each at the power that recovers nine carriers in ten, against the maximum of its own control ring. Marker shape is the band, open symbols the compact array, a cross a channel narrower than 200\,kHz, and arrows the three windows that never reach ninety per cent. The line and band are the noise-dominated value and its spread, the dotted line the single factor fitted to all of them. \emph  {(b)}\nobreakspace  {}The two strata's recovery curves: solid as the screen is applied, dashed with the star's own leak into the ring removed, which is a diagnostic and not the test used here. The disc-affected pair lie on top of one another.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:strata}{{1}{2}{Why the completeness is quoted in two strata. \emph {(a)}~The \StrNInjWin {} directly injected Class~A windows, each at the power that recovers nine carriers in ten, against the maximum of its own control ring. Marker shape is the band, open symbols the compact array, a cross a channel narrower than 200\,kHz, and arrows the three windows that never reach ninety per cent. The line and band are the noise-dominated value and its spread, the dotted line the single factor fitted to all of them. \emph {(b)}~The two strata's recovery curves: solid as the screen is applied, dashed with the star's own leak into the ring removed, which is a diagnostic and not the test used here. The disc-affected pair lie on top of one another}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \emph  {(a)}\nobreakspace  {}Class\nobreakspace  {}A sensitivity: the cumulative number of systems whose best window reaches a given $\mathrm  {EIRP}_{90}$, the power at which nine carriers in ten are recovered through the trigger and the spatial screen together. The shaded band is the combined interval of Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:p90budget}. \emph  {(b)}\nobreakspace  {}The temporal selection function: systems grouped by the longest separation between their searched epochs, an independent epoch being a separation of more than 1{} day. \textbf  {For the 27{} systems observed in a single block, and the 13{} whose blocks all fall within one day --- left of the dashed line --- independent confirmation was not possible at all}, whatever the sensitivity in panel\nobreakspace  {}(a). Recurrence over years can be tested for 23{} systems of 82.}}{2}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:classasens}{{2}{2}{\emph {(a)}~Class~A sensitivity: the cumulative number of systems whose best window reaches a given $\mathrm {EIRP}_{90}$, the power at which nine carriers in ten are recovered through the trigger and the spatial screen together. The shaded band is the combined interval of Table~\ref {tab:p90budget}. \emph {(b)}~The temporal selection function: systems grouped by the longest separation between their searched epochs, an independent epoch being a separation of more than \EpSep {} day. \textbf {For the \EpOne {} systems observed in a single block, and the \EpSameDay {} whose blocks all fall within one day --- left of the dashed line --- independent confirmation was not possible at all}, whatever the sensitivity in panel~(a). Recurrence over years can be tested for \EpYears {} systems of \EpTot }{figure.2}{}}
